ove yourself so  quickly that you can do it so easily as  well  yeah awesome so let let's end on this  then obviously you from what i can see  you graduated union in 2020  a lot of young people enter the the  recruitment industry a lot of people  find this podcast and it helps them  understand if it's a career for them  we've spoken about the challenges  there's been plenty of lows  but you've uh you've uh rode through  that you've worked through it and  can tell see sort of how energized you  are and  obviously whenever we suppose you seem  super happy and engaged so like  hopefully this can showcase people like  yes it is difficult yes it is  challenging but the sort of hard times  and the people you're doing it with and  the actual job itself overall in the  long term  it's all worth it but like why do you  think  more young people why do you think more  people should actually consider  recruitment as a career choice a lot of  people fall into it as an accident have  no [ __ ] clue about it but like why  should people actually identify as a  career that they want to get into from  from your perspective  yeah i think it's really funny because  i'd only had started hearing about  recruitment while i was at uni and i  this is really bad but i i remember  speaking to one of my friends and i was  like oh my god i'd never go into  recruitment like it's such a like  scapegoat of a career  and like  like a scapegoat of crayola i thought  like oh you can't get a job after you  need to go into recruitment like that is  really bad like that was my that was  like my mentality of it while i was at  uni and then i  like i basically just like started  eating my words i got into recruiting my  friend was like hannah do you remember  what you said i was like yeah i do yeah  yeah this is really where i was like but  when you like when you actually find out  more about it and realize that it's  actually quite difficult like it's not  it's not this like easy thing that you  just do 